NonConstMethodOnConstReceiver is single-file by construction: the emit site is gated on file_classes, so a const receiver whose class lives in another file is silently unchecked


## Reported by lane-resolver, 2026-08-31, as a by-product of the B114 audit

## The mechanism, and it is short enough to check by reading

- `file_const_methods` is built ONLY by `index_file_classes`, which walks **one
  document**.
- The sole `NonConstMethodOnConstReceiver` emit site sits inside the
  `if let Some((_, members)) = self.file_classes.get(&type_name)` arm — also
  **one document**.

So the gate is `file_classes`, not the const set.

## Repro

`a.as`:

    class C { void Mutate() {} }

`b.as`:

    void f(const C@ c) { c.Mutate(); }

**Same file: this diagnoses**, and that is game parity — confirmed against
`HatDump.as:60`.

**Split across files: silent.** `file_classes` has no entry for `C`, the arm is
never entered, and control falls through to `lookup_method_return`, whose own
comment already concedes "External types: no const-qualifier metadata yet".

## Why this is NOT closed by B114, despite looking like it should be

B114 pools `is_const` and makes the metadata available cross-file. That is
necessary and not sufficient: **the gate is `file_classes`, not the const set.**
A pooled `is_const` sitting in a `Symbol` changes nothing while the emit site is
still inside an arm that only single-file classes can enter.

Do not close this as a duplicate of B114, and do not assume landing B114
silently fixed it — check the arm.

## The cost of closing it, which is why this is its own ticket

Closing it means letting the rule fire on symbols resolved from the **pool**.
That is a new false-positive surface: the rule currently only ever sees classes
this LSP parsed itself, and pool symbols include engine types where the
const-qualifier story is exactly the "no metadata yet" case above. B101 added
method constness to the pooled symbol, so the data exists — but "the data
exists" and "the data is right for every provenance" are different claims and
only the second licenses the change.

**Wants its own measurement before its own fix:** instrument the widened gate to
count how many additional emits it would produce across the 151-plugin fleet,
and read the disagreements, before writing anything. A zero delta here would be
suspicious rather than reassuring — the whole point is that it should fire more.